  "critical_note": "Internal combustion engines enable motorized transport, aviation, and portable power generation that steam engines cannot practically provide",
  "description": "Otto cycle (gasoline, spark ignition) and Diesel cycle (compression ignition) engines converting fuel combustion into rotary mechanical power. Gasoline engines achieve 25-35% efficiency at 0.5-5 kW/kg. Diesel engines achieve 35-45% efficiency (up to 50% marine) with higher torque and longer life. Requires precision machining at 10-25 μm tolerances.",
